# Every text file is LF, in the index and in the working tree.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so without this
# file an untouched Windows clone checks the tree out as CRLF and then fails the
# repository's own checks. Measured in issue #415: `vp check` reports format
# failures throughout a clone with no source changes, and the fixture test in
# tools/oracle/analyze-rail-box-orientation.test.mjs compares the analyzer's LF
# output against the fixture's 470 CRLF lines.
#
# `eol=lf` is the load-bearing half. `text=auto` on its own normalizes what goes
# into the index but still checks out the platform's native ending, which is the
# ending the tools break on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, stated rather than left to inference. `text=auto` reaches the same
# answer from their content, but packages/exporter/basisu has no extension to go
# by, and a wrong guess on any of these corrupts the file on checkout.
*.basis binary
*.exe   binary
*.png   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
packages/exporter/basisu* binary
